urname>Boreham</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Thun</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Heath</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mortality from tobacco in developed countries: indirect estimation from national vital statistics</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1992</year><volume>339</volume><fpage>1268</fpage><lpage>1278</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1349675</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b5-ijerph-06-00069"><label>5.</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>US Department of Health and Human Services</collab><source>Best practices for comprehensive tobacco-control programs</source><publisher-name>Department of Health and Human Services, Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, National Center for Chronic Disease Prevention and Health Promotion, Office on Smoking and Health</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Atlanta, U.S</publisher-loc><year>2007</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/tobacco/tobacco_control_programs/stateandcommunity/best_practices/">http://www.cdc.gov/tobacco/tobacco_control_programs/stateandcommunity/best_practices/</ext-link> (accessed December 12, 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b6-ijerph-06-00069"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>US Department of Health and Human Services</collab><source>Reducing the health consequences of smoking - 25 years of progress: a report of the Surgeon General</source><publisher-name>Department of Health and Human Services, Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, National Center for Chronic Disease Prevention and Health Promotion, Office on Smoking and Health</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Atlanta, GA, U.S</publisher-loc><year>1989</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://profiles.nlm.nih.gov/NN/B/B/X/S/">http://profiles.nlm.nih.gov/NN/B/B/X/S/</ext-link> (accessed December 12, 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b7-ijerph-06-00069"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>US Department of Health and Human Services</collab><source>The health consequences of Smoking &#x02013; Nicotine addiction; a report of the Surgeon General</source><publisher-name>Department of Health and Human Services, Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, National Center for Chronic Disease Prevention and Health Promotion, Office on Smoking and Health</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Atlanta, GA, U.S</publisher-loc><year>1988</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://profiles.nlm.nih.gov/NN/B/B/Z/D/_/nnbbzd.pdf">http://profiles.nlm.nih.gov/NN/B/B/Z/D/_/nnbbzd.pdf</ext-link> (accessed December 12, 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b8-ijerph-06-00069"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benowitz</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pharmacology of nicotine: addiction and therapeutics</article-title><source>Annu. Rev. Pharmacol. Toxicol</source><year>1996</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>597</fpage><lpage>613</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8725403</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ijerph-06-00069"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>CBS News</collab><source>Battling Big Tobacco: Mike Wallace talks to the highest-ranking tobacco whistleblower</source><publisher-name>CBS Worldwide Inc</publisher-name><publisher-name>New York, U.S</publisher-name><year>2005</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cbsnews.com/stories/2005/01/13/60II/main666867.shtml">http://www.cbsnews.com/stories/2005/01/13/60II/main666867.shtml</ext-link> (accessed December 12, 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b10-ijerph-06-00069"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mathers</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Loncar</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Projection of global mortality and burden of disease from 2002 to 2030</article-title><source>PLoS Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>e442</fpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://medicine.plosjournals.org/perlserv/?request=get-document&#x00026;doi=10.1371/journal.pmed.0030442&#x00026;ct=1">http://medicine.plosjournals.org/perlserv/?request=get-document&#x00026;doi=10.1371/journal.pmed.0030442&#x00026;ct=1</ext-link> (accessed December 12, 2008).<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17132052</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ijerph-06-00069"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>World Health Organization</collab><source>World health statistics</source><publisher-name>World Health Organization</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Geneva</publisher-loc><year>2008</year> Accessed 12/12/08 from (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/whosis/whostat/EN_WHS08_Full.pdf">http://www.who.int/whosis/whostat/EN_WHS08_Full.pdf</ext-link>).</citation></ref><ref id="b12-ijerph-06-00069"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Peto</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Smoking and death: the past 40 years and the next 40</article-title><source>Br. Med. J</source><year>1994</year><volume>309</volume><fpage>937</fpage><lpage>939</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7950669</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ijerph-06-00069"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thankappan</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Thresia</surname><given-names>CU</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tobacco use &#x00026; social status in Kerala</article-title><source>Indian J. Med. Res</source><year>2007</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://findarticles.com/p/articles/mi_qa3867/is_200710/ai_n21279010/pg_1?tag=artBody;col1">http://findarticles.com/p/articles/mi_qa3867/is_200710/ai_n21279010/pg_1?tag=artBody;col1</ext-link> (accessed December 12, 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b14-ijerph-06-00069"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MacKenzie</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Collin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The tobacco industry documents: an introductory handbook and resource guide for researchers</article-title><source>London Sch. Hyg. Trop. Med</source><year>2008</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.lshtm.ac.uk/cgch/tobacco/industry_docs.htm">http://www.lshtm.ac.uk/cgch/tobacco/industry_docs.htm</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ijerph-06-00069"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cummings</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Morley</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hyland</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Horan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Steger</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Leavell</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Marketing to America&#x02019;s youth: evidence from corporate documents</article-title><source>Tob. Control</source><year>2002</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>i5</fpage><lpage>i17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11893810</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ijerph-06-00069"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Perry</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The tobacco industry and underage youth smoking: Tobacco industry documents from the Minnesota litigation</article-title><source>Arch. Pediatr. Adolesc. Med</sourc